<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<dxl:DXLMessage xmlns:dxl="http://greengagedb.org/dxl/2010/12/">
  <dxl:Comment><![CDATA[

  Objective: with optimizer_enable_associativity off, ORCA explores the
  JoinAssociativity xform only if the total number of children of the n-ary
  joins with at least three children each in the query is at most
  optimizer_join_arity_for_associativity (JoinArityForAssociativity hint).
  The query has n-ary joins of 4 and 3 children, the total 7 is above the
  hint (5), so JoinAssociativity is disabled. ORCA keeps the join order of
  the query text for big and joins it last by a Hash Join over a Seq Scan,
  although the first branch alone would get an Index NLJ into big.

  Setup (3 segments):

  create table a   as select x, x % 10 + 1 as y, x % 10 + 1 as z
                      from generate_series(1, 1000) x distributed by (x);
  create table b   as select x as y from generate_series(1, 10) x distributed by (y);
  create table c   as select x as z from generate_series(1, 10) x distributed by (z);
  create table big as select x from generate_series(1, 100000) x distributed by (x);
  create index on a(x); create index on big(x);
  analyze a; analyze b; analyze c; analyze big;
  set allow_system_table_mods = on;
  update pg_class set reltuples = 10000000 where oid = 'big'::regclass;
  reset allow_system_table_mods;

  explain select count(*) from a join b using (y) join c using (z) join big using (x)
  where a.x > 900
  union all
  select count(*) from a join b using (y) join c using (z);

]]></dxl:Comment>
